{"name":"Movie Star","hex":"#c52033","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"movie star","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A leading actor in a movie, especially one perceived as a celebrity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/movie_star"}],"entries":[{"title":"Moviestar (Harpo song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Moviestar\" is a song written and recorded by Swedish singer-songwriter Harpo. Following two hit singles on Tio i Topp, Harpo wrote the song while sitting by his window, dedicating it to a friend of his that had aspirations of becoming an actor. \"Moviestar\" tells the story of an individual who believes they are an A-list actor in the league of Steve McQueen and James Dean, when instead it is revealed that they have only acted in a television advertisement. It makes multiple references to popular culture, including movie producer Ingmar Bergman."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Harpo_Movistar_Se.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moviestar_(Harpo_song)"},{"title":"Moviestar (Stereophonics song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Moviestar\" is a song by Welsh rock band Stereophonics, included on later editions of their fourth studio album, You Gotta Go There to Come Back. It was released as the fourth and final single from the album and was the first Stereophonics single released following the sacking of drummer Stuart Cable. The single peaked at number five on the UK Singles Chart, number 26 on the Irish Singles Chart, and number 85 on the Dutch Top 100."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7b/MoviestarStereophonics.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moviestar_(Stereophonics_song)"},{"title":"Movie star","blocks":[{"text":"A movie star is an actor who is famous for their starring, or leading, roles in movies. The term is used for performers who are marketable stars as they become popular household names and whose names are used to promote movies, for example in trailers and posters. The most prominent movie stars are known in the industry as bankable stars."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Movie_star"},{"title":"Film","blocks":[{"text":"A film, movie, or motion picture is a work of visual art that simulates experiences and otherwise communicates ideas, stories, perceptions, emotions, or atmosphere through the use of moving images that are generally, since the 1930s, synchronized with sound and sometimes feature other sensory stimuli."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Le_Voyage_dans_la_Lune_%281902%29.webm/330px--Le_Voyage_dans_la_Lune_%281902%29.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Film"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Bengt_Palmers_1982.jpg/250px-Bengt_Palmers_1982.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/45/Bengt_Palmers_1982.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Bengt_Palmers_1982.jpg/250px-Bengt_Palmers_1982.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bengt Palmers produced and wrote arrangements for the song.[11]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABengt_Palmers_1982.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3d/Harpo_Moviestar_Gold_Record.jpg/330px-Harpo_Moviestar_Gold_Record.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3d/Harpo_Moviestar_Gold_Record.jpg/330px-Harpo_Moviestar_Gold_Record.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A press-party for \"Moviestar\" after it sold gold. Harpo a